    "body": "# What does this PR do ?\n\nApplies the Hugging Face YaRN defaults (`beta_fast=32`, `beta_slow=1`, `truncate=True`) in the shared HF → Megatron config mapping when a YaRN `rope_scaling` omits them, so GPT-family checkpoints with YaRN no longer crash at model construction.\n\n**The bug:** the shared mapping only copies YaRN keys that are present. A config such as `{\"rope_type\": \"yarn\", \"factor\": 4.0, \"original_max_position_embeddings\": 32768}` is the standard form for Qwen2.5 / Qwen3 long context. With it, `yarn_beta_fast` / `yarn_beta_slow` stay `None`. Megatron Core's `GPTModel` passes these fields to `YarnRotaryEmbedding` explicitly, which overrides its defaults, so model construction fails:\n\n```\nTypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for *: 'NoneType' and 'int'   (yarn_rotary_pos_embedding.py:244)\n```\n\n# Changelog\n\n- `MegatronModelBridge.YARN_HF_DEFAULTS`: the defaults transformers' `_compute_yarn_parameters` uses for omitted keys.\n- The GPT YaRN branch of the shared mapping fills those defaults with `setdefault`. Values the checkpoint sets explicitly always win.\n- Unit tests: defaults are filled for omitted keys, explicit keys are preserved, and non-YaRN configs are unaffected.\n- `Qwen3Bridge`: drops its local copy of the same three defaults, added by #6365, now that the shared mapping fills them. Qwen3's existing YaRN tests, which assert 32 / 1 / `True` for omitted keys and keep explicit values, now cover the shared path.\n\n# Scope and behaviour change\n\n- **Affected:** generic GPT bridges whose YaRN config goes through the shared mapping (for example Qwen2/2.5, Qwen3, Qwen3-MoE).\n- **Not affected:**\n  - MLA models (separate `MLA_ROPE_SCALING_MAPPING` branch).\n  - Mistral and Ministral3, which build their providers by hand.\n  - GPT-OSS, which sets every YaRN field explicitly after the mapping.\n- **Behaviour change for configs that already worked:** a YaRN config that sets the betas but omits `truncate` previously got `yarn_correction_range_round_to_int=None` (no rounding). It now gets `True`, matching Hugging Face's default. Agreement with HF logits improves (table below).\n\n# Verification\n\nProvider path (`AutoBridge.to_megatron_provider()`), tiny random-weight checkpoints, single GPU, logits compared with Hugging Face on the same input:\n\n| HF `rope_scaling` | `main` | this PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| Qwen2, YaRN, no betas | `TypeError` at construction | builds; cosine 0.999993, argmax 100% |\n| Qwen3, YaRN, no betas | `TypeError` at construction | builds; cosine 0.999989, argmax 100% |\n| Qwen2, YaRN, betas set, no `truncate` | cosine 0.999980, argmax 99.2% | cosine 0.999993, argmax 100% |\n\n- `tests/unit_tests/models/test_model_bridge.py`: 57 passed.\n- Regression run (GPT provider, Ministral3, GPT-OSS, StepFun, DeepSeek, Qwen, Llama, AutoBridge): 555 passed, 1 skipped.\n- `ruff check` / `ruff format --check`: clean (ruff 0.16.7; `pre-commit` itself not run).\n- After rebasing onto `main` (Megatron Core 8949def81) and removing the Qwen3 copy: 564 passed, 1 skipped across `test_model_bridge.py`, `models/qwen`, `recipes/qwen`, `test_transformer_config.py`, `test_gpt_provider.py`, and the DeepSeek, Ministral3, Kimi K2.5-VL, StepFun and GPT-OSS model tests.\n\n# Before your PR is \"Ready for review\"\n\n**Pre checks**:\n\n- [x] Make sure you read and followed [Contributor guidelines](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] Did you write any new necessary tests?\n- [ ] Did you add or update any necessary documentation?\n- [ ] Does the PR affect components that are optional to install? (Ex: Numba, Pynini, Apex etc)\n  - [ ] Reviewer: Does the PR have correct import guards for all optional libraries?\n\n# Additional Information\n\n- #6365 (merged) added the same three defaults locally in `Qwen3Bridge`; this PR, merging second, removes that copy.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
